    "result_text": "The build is green \u2014 the only test in the suite passes. Here's what I implemented for the `salutation` feature.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec: *the request may include `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR); return `salutation` = `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.*\n\nSince this project generates its DTOs from the OpenAPI spec and wires MapStruct to map entity\u2194DTO by property name, I added the field to the spec and the entity and let the generators do the rest:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**\n   - Added `title` (optional input string) to the `OwnerFields` schema.\n   - Added `salutation` (derived, `readOnly`) to the `Owner` response schema.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (`model`)\n   - Added a persisted `title` column (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter.\n   - Added derived `getSalutation()` \u2014 `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when the title is null/blank. This follows the existing derived-field convention (like `getDisplayName()`/`getInitials()`).\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `title` column to all four dialects (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) so the persisted field has a home. The tests run against `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema column is required there.\n\nThe generated `OwnerMapperImpl` now maps `owner.getTitle()`/`setTitle()` both directions and `owner.getSalutation()` into the response DTO, so `POST /api/owners` accepts `title` and `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns `salutation`.\n\nVerification: `AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` (posts `title=DR`, `lastName=who`, expects `$.salutation == \"DR who\"`) passes, and the full suite is **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
