        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is coherent, additive, and idiomatic for this codebase.\n\n- **Right unit.** `getSalutation()` derives from `title` (an `Owner`-specific column) and `lastName` (from `Person`). Because `title` lives on `Owner`, the derived method must live on `Owner` too \u2014 it can't move down to `Person` like `getInitials()`/`getDisplayName()`. The placement follows the established pattern of co-locating a derived accessor with the field it derives from (e.g. `getTelephoneDisplay()` sits next to `telephone`).\n\n- **Consistent with existing derived properties.** `Owner`/`Person` already expose a family of derived, non-persisted read methods (`getInitials`, `getDisplayName`, age band, membership level, region, timezone, identity key). Adding one more read-only derived getter, documented with the same javadoc style (\"Derived per response, not persisted.\"), is exactly what a maintainer would expect \u2014 not a new catch-all.\n\n- **No duplication / no logic misplaced.** The salutation rule is expressed once, in one small method; the null/blank guard is minimal and reads naturally. The description text repeated in the OpenAPI schema is documentation, not logic duplication.\n\n- **Field plumbing is uniform.** The `title` column is added to the entity and to all four dialect schemas (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) in the same relative position, and surfaced in `openapi.yml` next to the sibling derived `initials`/`fullName` properties as a `readOnly` field. Nothing is half-wired.\n\nNote: the spec concerns only request/response shaping, and this project routes through OfficeFloor function steps with DTOs at the edges. This diff only touches the entity + schema + OpenAPI; wiring `title` through the request DTO/response mapping (if not already handled) would be a correctness concern \u2014 out of scope for this structural review."
